    "title": "Train hits, kills person crossing railroad tracks in Redding - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jessica Skropanic ,\n1 days ago\nA pedestrian walking on railroad tracks in south Redding died late Monday afternoon after they were hit by a Union Pacific train, the Redding Police Department reported.\nWitnesses told police the person started to cross the train tracks that run next to Highway 273 — south of the South Bonnyview Road intersection — before 4:50 p.m. It appeared they were trying to dart across the track before the oncoming train arrived, Redding Police Cpl. Ben Omey said in the announcement.\nThe northbound train wasn't able to stop in time, Omey said, and the pedestrian didn't make it to the other side of the tracks before they were hit by the train.\nA medical team pronounced the person dead at the site of the crash, according to Omey's report.\nNote to readers: If you appreciate the work we do here at the Redding Record Searchlight, please consider subscribing yourself or giving the gift of a subscription to someone you know.\nRedding police didn't release the victim's name, age, or other information until relatives are contacted, Omey said.\nThe Shasta County Coroner's Office is also investigating the fatal crash.\nOmey urged people not to walk on railroad tracks and only cross railways at designated pedestrian crossings.\nJessica Skropanic is a features reporter for the Record Searchlight/USA Today Network. She covers science, arts, social issues and news stories. Follow her on Twitter @RS_JSkropanic and on Facebook . Join Jessica on Record Searchlight Facebook groups Get Out! Nor Cal , Today in Shasta County and Shaping Redding’s Future . To support and sustain this work, please subscribe today. Thank you.\nThis article originally appeared on Redding Record Searchlight: Train hits, kills person crossing railroad tracks in Redding\n7",
